.TH "BOOTSTRAP" "1" "2026-09-18" "bootstrap 202604240000-git" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bootstrap \- Bootstrap an RPM development container
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootstrap
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bootstrap
sets up an RPM development environment by installing required packages,
configuring the rpmbuild directory tree, copying /etc/skel files, and
downloading the .rpmmacros configuration file. It detects the system
package manager and installs the appropriate build tools for RPM or Debian-based systems.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Show script version and exit.
.TP
.B --no-skel
Skip copying /etc/skel files to /root.
.TP
.B --no-macros
Skip downloading .rpmmacros file.
.TP
.B --force-macros
Force download and overwrite .rpmmacros file even if it already exists.
.TP
.B --packages FILE
Read additional package names from FILE (one package per line).
Comments starting with # and empty lines are ignored.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any value, disables all colored output.
.TP
.B SHOW_RAW
When set to
.BR true ,
disables all colored output.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.B bootstrap
must be run as root (uid 0).
The system must have one of the following package managers installed:
.BR dnf (1),
.BR yum (1),
or
.BR apt-get (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.rpmmacros
RPM macro configuration file downloaded during bootstrap.
.TP
.B ~/.local/tmp/BUILD
RPM build directory (created if missing).
.TP
.B ~/.local/tmp/BUILDROOT
RPM buildroot directory (created if missing).
.TP
.B ~/rpmbuild
RPM root directory using flat per-package layout (created if missing).
.TP
.B /tmp/bootstrap.pid
Process ID file created during execution (cleaned up on exit).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Bootstrap with all defaults:
.B bootstrap
.TP
Bootstrap but skip skel copy:
.B bootstrap --no-skel
.TP
Bootstrap and install additional packages from a file:
.B bootstrap --packages /path/to/packages.txt
.TP
Bootstrap, skip macros download but force-download later:
.B bootstrap --no-macros
.br
.B bootstrap --force-macros
.SH NOTES
.B bootstrap
uses a flat rpmbuild layout where each package gets its own directory
(~/rpmbuild/{name}/{name}.spec + sources), not the traditional rpmdev-setuptree
structure with BUILD/BUILDROOT/RPMS/SOURCES/SPECS/SRPMS subdirectories.
